      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:09 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1293",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a1e6cbfa4ff34a8f154af2ea163074e966b923a8735b7a8d63a9d316d411c012",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a1e6cbfa4ff3-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Congress enacted 18 U.S.C. 1956(h) for the sole purpose of increasing the penalties for money laundering conspiracies."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1293",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a1e6cbfa4ff34a8f154af2ea163074e966b923a8735b7a8d63a9d316d411c012",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a1e6cbfa4ff3-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: Would you just clarify one thing for me? Did they have to prove an overt act in order to establish venue?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1293",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a1e6cbfa4ff34a8f154af2ea163074e966b923a8735b7a8d63a9d316d411c012",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a1e6cbfa4ff3-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Is that the only basis for venue? I mean, I thought the statute provides that's just one of the bases for venue."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1293",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a1e6cbfa4ff34a8f154af2ea163074e966b923a8735b7a8d63a9d316d411c012",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a1e6cbfa4ff3-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our position is that the venue provision in 1956, 1956(i), is the exclusive venue provision for money laundering."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1293",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a1e6cbfa4ff34a8f154af2ea163074e966b923a8735b7a8d63a9d316d411c012",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a1e6cbfa4ff3-0001-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF JONATHAN L. MARCUS ON BEHALF OF THE RESPONDENT"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1293",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a1e6cbfa4ff34a8f154af2ea163074e966b923a8735b7a8d63a9d316d411c012",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a1e6cbfa4ff3-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: When -- when you say when there are multiple objects, you're not getting the money -- money laundering just under 371. You'd surely charge both under 371 and under -- under -- what is it? 1956."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1293",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a1e6cbfa4ff34a8f154af2ea163074e966b923a8735b7a8d63a9d316d411c012",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a1e6cbfa4ff3-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Petitioners also argue that because prior to enactment of section 1956(h), the Government had to prosecute money laundering conspiracies for 6 years under section 371, that this Court should presume that Congress intended to perpetuate the overt act requirement of section 371 into the money laundering conspiracy offense."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1293",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "a1e6cbfa4ff34a8f154af2ea163074e966b923a8735b7a8d63a9d316d411c012",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a1e6cbfa4ff3-0002-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted.\n(Whereupon, at 10:49 a.m., the case in the\nabove-entitled matter was submitted.)"
    }
  ],
